{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792961768,"nonce":"RPBI4trV+LPpE271NhdFbN8amZE=","title":"Keep the editor minimap flush with its pane edges","message":"The code editor's context menu wrapper inherits align-self:flex-start from the generic dropdown root, shrinking the editor to its intrinsic width. A measured 946px tab page only contains a 702px code editor, leaving 244px to its right. The minimap is flush with that smaller editor, rather than the pane. The full-width breadcrumb row also leaves a 28px blank strip above the map.\n\nStretch the context wrapper to its pane and let CodeEditor accept a header in its text column, so the breadcrumb sits beside the minimap. Keep the map's canvas/slider scaled to the full strip while scroll calculations use the actual text viewport. Verify resizing, tab switches and both split orientations in both themes, preserving context-menu behavior.","files":null}]}